    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completion\n\n### Description\n\n#### The problem\n\nAfter starting typing, a popup window with suggestions appear, this is quite useful, but if the word is completed *by hand* the window does not disappear and `<Enter>` has to be pressed (e.g. if there a new line should be inserted) -- this is uncomfortable -- could it auto-dissapear in case of a word typed in whole and without any possibilities of continuation?\n\n#### Example\n\n(When coding `Python`)\n\n    value = None\n\n\n    def fun():\n        return val  # <- here the popup remains,\n        #           #    even if no other option for completion is available\n\n\nIs there a possibility of self-closing popup? Or perhaps I'm missing something in the configuration of mini.completion?\n\n    $ nvim -V1 -v   \n    NVIM v0.11.5\n    Build type: Release\n    LuaJIT 2.1.1741730670\n\n       system vimrc file: \"$VIM/sysinit.vim\"\n      fall-back for $VIM: \"/usr/local/share/nvim\"\n\nFrom mini.nvim CHANGELOG.md (cloned repo): `Version 0.18.0-dev`",
